chitecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S12\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S13\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":10418}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S12\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S12_DATA_REUNIFICATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"cfaab1b39c0a343b59df16ac55b645b94a08b758252b50b972f25daabdb3d0a9\",\"source_size_bytes\":5433,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Evacuee accountability, privacy, and reunification\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe operation needs household status, transport assignment, shelter check-in, and reunification contact. Medical accommodations are restricted and may not appear in the public missing-person feed.\nThe minimum retention period is seven days after incident closure; operational rosters must be deleted within thirty days unless a legal hold applies. The last exercise retained exported spreadsheets for ninety-two days.\nA person may be safe but not at a county shelter. Accountability must accept verified self-evacuation without publishing a destination or health status.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTransport and shelter effects should update one private accountability record, but public reporting must use aggregated status. S07 medical matching consumes restricted fields under public-health authority.\nA plan mutation to identifiers, export, or retention invalidates the prior privacy check.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | data class | collection | retention | access | status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| DATA-000 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 7d | operational | deletion-proof-missing |\n| DATA-001 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 8d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-002 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 9d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-003 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 10d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-004 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 11d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-005 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 12d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-006 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 13d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-007 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 14d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-008 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 15d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-009 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 16d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-010 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 17d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-011 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 18d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-012 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 19d | operational | deletion-proof-missing |\n| DATA-013 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 20d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-014 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 21d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-015 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 22d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-016 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 23d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-017 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 24d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-018 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 25d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-019 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 26d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-020 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 27d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-021 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 28d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-022 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 29d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-023 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 30d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-024 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 7d | operational | deletion-proof-missing |\n| DATA-025 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 8d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-026 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 9d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-027 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 10d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-028 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 11d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-029 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 12d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-030 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 13d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-031 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 14d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-032 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 15d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-033 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 16d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-034 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 17d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-035 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 18d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-036 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 19d | restricted | deletion-proof-missing |\n| DATA-037 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 20d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-038 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 21d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-039 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 22d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-040 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 23d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-041 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 24d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-042 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 25d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-043 | shelter-checkin | minimum-necessary | 26d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-044 | reunification-contact | minimum-necessary | 27d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-045 | household-status | minimum-necessary | 28d | operational | complete |\n| DATA-046 | medical-accommodation | minimum-necessary | 29d | restricted | complete |\n| DATA-047 | transport-assignment | minimum-necessary | 30d | operational | complete |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nSpecify minimum fields, access roles, reconciliation, deletion proof, and public/private separation.\nDo not equate shelter check-in with complete zone accountability.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S13\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S13_EXERCISE_REVIEW.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"56498133050c8c08dcf8661d0c4c83d972d56b3da4ab119802ed179bac2715a3\",\"source_size_bytes\":4510,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Full-scale exercise defects and repair evidence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nExercise Cedar-6 achieved only 1,180 vehicles per hour at Mill Junction, delayed lift-bus dispatch by ninety-six minutes, and accounted for 91 percent of households by the six-hour mark.\nCounty radio voice worked, but volunteer unit identifiers did not cross the gateway. Civic Arena opened, while Ridge School's filter test failed and fuel arrived after seventeen hours.\nA corrective-action spreadsheet marks several items closed based on owner attestation. Readiness requires current execution evidence for the exact plan rather than a status label.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nThe observed exercise values override nominal road, fleet, communications, shelter, and fuel targets until a repair is rechecked. One exercise therefore links several evidence domains.\nChanging the zone order or fleet roster after a repair makes the old exercise only historical evidence.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | defect | zone | delay | status | exercise binding |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| EX-000 | merge-throughput | A-North | 38m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-001 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 51m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-002 | radio-handoff | B-East | 64m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-003 | family-accountability | B-Center | 77m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-004 | shelter-filter | C-South | 90m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-005 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 103m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-006 | merge-throughput | A-North | 116m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-007 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 129m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-008 | radio-handoff | B-East | 142m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-009 | family-accountability | B-Center | 155m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-010 | shelter-filter | C-South | 49m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-011 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 62m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-012 | merge-throughput | A-North | 75m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-013 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 88m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-014 | radio-handoff | B-East | 101m | open | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-015 | family-accountability | B-Center | 114m | repaired | exercise-r3 |\n| EX-016 | shelter-filter | C-South | 127m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-017 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 140m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-018 | merge-throughput | A-North | 153m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-019 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 47m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-020 | radio-handoff | B-East | 60m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-021 | family-accountability | B-Center | 73m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-022 | shelter-filter | C-South | 86m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-023 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 99m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-024 | merge-throughput | A-North | 112m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-025 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 125m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-026 | radio-handoff | B-East | 138m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-027 | family-accountability | B-Center | 151m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-028 | shelter-filter | C-South | 45m | open | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-029 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 58m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-030 | merge-throughput | A-North | 71m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-031 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 84m | repaired | exercise-r4 |\n| EX-032 | radio-handoff | B-East | 97m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-033 | family-accountability | B-Center | 110m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-034 | shelter-filter | C-South | 123m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-035 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 136m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-036 | merge-throughput | A-North | 149m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-037 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 43m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-038 | radio-handoff | B-East | 56m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-039 | family-accountability | B-Center | 69m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-040 | shelter-filter | C-South | 82m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-041 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 95m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-042 | merge-throughput | A-North | 108m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-043 | lift-dispatch | A-River | 121m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-044 | radio-handoff | B-East | 134m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-045 | family-accountability | B-Center | 147m | repaired | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-046 | shelter-filter | C-South | 41m | open | exercise-r5 |\n| EX-047 | fuel-arrival | C-Ridge | 54m | open | exercise-r5 |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nCarry every material exercise defect into the plan with owner, repair, current recheck, and blocking status.\nDo not count owner attestation as operational proof.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"accepted\":false,\"configuration_id\":\"A1_COUPLED\",\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"input_result_id\":\"RESULT-012\",\"output_sha256\":\"7265df8adaf18c70c485574c6f1586f1c4b1cbc92fda06966de218e8cee7489b\",\"schema\":\"artifact-coupled-maintenance-rejection-v0\",\"validation_code\":\"token_budget_exceeded\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S15\",\"start_line\":1}] }<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S14:1-70+S15:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"e9d75f4a73b35f3a549e775401c205d8e7efd933d7c801fddfb31110b7b30a59\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-015\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S15\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":9387}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S14\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S14_COST_CONTRACTS.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"b01cae551ccb98947a3db2365ff446f9595bf97fa50448db7d859c6ada50a3b2\",\"source_size_bytes\":4743,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Emergency contracts, cost ceilings, and procurement authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe incident commander may authorize up to $750,000 of life-safety expenditure without board approval. The current forty-eight-hour plan is estimated at $612,000 before animal overflow and alternate fuel supply.\nThe lowest-cost bus vendor cannot provide lift-equipped vehicles. The alternate fuel supplier costs 18 percent more but uses County 12 instead of smoke-prone South Pass.\nCost optimization may not remove a hard accessibility, medical, communications, or continuity control. Costs beyond authority require escalation but do not justify silently declaring an unsafe plan ready.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nContract choices alter fleet accessibility and fuel-route resilience. They must appear in the same candidate effects and checks as the operational plan.\nMigration-only or incident-only costs need a retirement condition so temporary capacity does not become ungoverned standing spend.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | category | units | cost | authority | contract |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| COST-000 | bus-callout | 4 | $1800 | incident-authority-required | contract-r4 |\n| COST-001 | accessible-cot | 5 | $1937 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-002 | filter-bank | 6 | $2074 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-003 | fuel-staging | 7 | $2211 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-004 | animal-trailer | 8 | $2348 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-005 | translation | 9 | $2485 | incident-authority-required | contract-r4 |\n| COST-006 | bus-callout | 10 | $2622 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-007 | accessible-cot | 11 | $2759 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-008 | filter-bank | 12 | $2896 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-009 | fuel-staging | 13 | $3033 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-010 | animal-trailer | 14 | $3170 | incident-authority-required | contract-r4 |\n| COST-011 | translation | 15 | $3307 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-012 | bus-callout | 16 | $3444 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-013 | accessible-cot | 4 | $3581 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-014 | filter-bank | 5 | $3718 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-015 | fuel-staging | 6 | $3855 | incident-authority-required | contract-r4 |\n| COST-016 | animal-trailer | 7 | $3992 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-017 | translation | 8 | $4129 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-018 | bus-callout | 9 | $4266 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-019 | accessible-cot | 10 | $4403 | preapproved | contract-r4 |\n| COST-020 | filter-bank | 11 | $4540 | incident-authority-required | contract-r5 |\n| COST-021 | fuel-staging | 12 | $4677 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-022 | animal-trailer | 13 | $4814 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-023 | translation | 14 | $4951 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-024 | bus-callout | 15 | $5088 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-025 | accessible-cot | 16 | $5225 | incident-authority-required | contract-r5 |\n| COST-026 | filter-bank | 4 | $5362 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-027 | fuel-staging | 5 | $5499 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-028 | animal-trailer | 6 | $5636 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-029 | translation | 7 | $5773 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-030 | bus-callout | 8 | $5910 | incident-authority-required | contract-r5 |\n| COST-031 | accessible-cot | 9 | $6047 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-032 | filter-bank | 10 | $6184 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-033 | fuel-staging | 11 | $6321 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-034 | animal-trailer | 12 | $6458 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-035 | translation | 13 | $6595 | incident-authority-required | contract-r5 |\n| COST-036 | bus-callout | 14 | $6732 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-037 | accessible-cot | 15 | $6869 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-038 | filter-bank | 16 | $7006 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-039 | fuel-staging | 4 | $7143 | preapproved | contract-r5 |\n| COST-040 | animal-trailer | 5 | $7280 | incident-authority-required | contract-r6 |\n| COST-041 | translation | 6 | $7417 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n| COST-042 | bus-callout | 7 | $7554 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n| COST-043 | accessible-cot | 8 | $7691 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n| COST-044 | filter-bank | 9 | $7828 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n| COST-045 | fuel-staging | 10 | $7965 | incident-authority-required | contract-r6 |\n| COST-046 | animal-trailer | 11 | $8102 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n| COST-047 | translation | 12 | $8239 | preapproved | contract-r6 |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nState the cost envelope, authority, contingency, and controls that cannot be traded away.\nTreat price, capability, route, and activation time as a joint selection.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S15\",\"source_path\":\"cedar_sources/S15_WEATHER_ENSEMBLE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"c4a8a9397f8b73ee2575405d377081eadaa4a7340339eb8db1b59c330027cdc6\",\"source_size_bytes\":4172,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Wind-shift ensemble and forecast update cadence\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nForecasts update every ninety minutes. The base case keeps the fire north of Zone B, but 42 percent of current ensemble members shift winds after 16:00 and shorten Zone A arrival below six hours.\nA later update can improve the median while widening the worst-case range. The trigger uses the conservative operational envelope until field observations rule out the adverse branch.\nAircraft infrared mapping can lag by two hours under smoke. Absence of a new perimeter is not proof that fire spread stopped.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nOrder timing in S01–S02, road viability in S04, and air quality in S11 all depend on the same forecast revision. Mixing revisions produces an incoherent plan.\nThe verification packet must name the forecast cycle and expire it at the next update or material field observation.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | cycle | wind | shift probability | arrival | envelope |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| WX-000 | cycle-00 | 14mph | 18% | 4.5h | base-case |\n| WX-001 | cycle-01 | 19mph | 29% | 5.0h | base-case |\n| WX-002 | cycle-02 | 24mph | 40% | 5.4h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-003 | cycle-03 | 29mph | 51% | 5.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-004 | cycle-04 | 34mph | 62% | 6.3h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-005 | cycle-05 | 39mph | 73% | 6.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-006 | cycle-06 | 44mph | 21% | 7.2h | base-case |\n| WX-007 | cycle-07 | 18mph | 32% | 7.7h | base-case |\n| WX-008 | cycle-08 | 23mph | 43% | 8.1h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-009 | cycle-09 | 28mph | 54% | 8.6h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-010 | cycle-10 | 33mph | 65% | 9.0h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-011 | cycle-11 | 38mph | 76% | 9.4h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-012 | cycle-12 | 43mph | 24% | 4.5h | base-case |\n| WX-013 | cycle-13 | 17mph | 35% | 5.0h | base-case |\n| WX-014 | cycle-14 | 22mph | 46% | 5.4h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-015 | cycle-15 | 27mph | 57% | 5.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-016 | cycle-16 | 32mph | 68% | 6.3h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-017 | cycle-17 | 37mph | 79% | 6.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-018 | cycle-18 | 42mph | 27% | 7.2h | base-case |\n| WX-019 | cycle-19 | 16mph | 38% | 7.7h | base-case |\n| WX-020 | cycle-20 | 21mph | 49% | 8.1h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-021 | cycle-21 | 26mph | 60% | 8.6h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-022 | cycle-22 | 31mph | 71% | 9.0h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-023 | cycle-23 | 36mph | 19% | 9.4h | base-case |\n| WX-024 | cycle-24 | 41mph | 30% | 4.5h | base-case |\n| WX-025 | cycle-25 | 15mph | 41% | 5.0h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-026 | cycle-26 | 20mph | 52% | 5.4h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-027 | cycle-27 | 25mph | 63% | 5.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-028 | cycle-28 | 30mph | 74% | 6.3h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-029 | cycle-29 | 35mph | 22% | 6.8h | base-case |\n| WX-030 | cycle-30 | 40mph | 33% | 7.2h | base-case |\n| WX-031 | cycle-31 | 14mph | 44% | 7.7h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-032 | cycle-32 | 19mph | 55% | 8.1h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-033 | cycle-33 | 24mph | 66% | 8.6h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-034 | cycle-34 | 29mph | 77% | 9.0h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-035 | cycle-35 | 34mph | 25% | 9.4h | base-case |\n| WX-036 | cycle-36 | 39mph | 36% | 4.5h | base-case |\n| WX-037 | cycle-37 | 44mph | 47% | 5.0h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-038 | cycle-38 | 18mph | 58% | 5.4h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-039 | cycle-39 | 23mph | 69% | 5.8h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-040 | cycle-40 | 28mph | 80% | 6.3h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-041 | cycle-41 | 33mph | 28% | 6.8h | base-case |\n| WX-042 | cycle-42 | 38mph | 39% | 7.2h | base-case |\n| WX-043 | cycle-43 | 43mph | 50% | 7.7h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-044 | cycle-44 | 17mph | 61% | 8.1h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-045 | cycle-45 | 22mph | 72% | 8.6h | conservative-envelope |\n| WX-046 | cycle-46 | 27mph | 20% | 9.0h | base-case |\n| WX-047 | cycle-47 | 32mph | 31% | 9.4h | base-case |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nBind decisions to one forecast cycle and state expiry and adverse-branch actions.\nDo not cancel protective actions from a better median alone.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"accepted\":false,\"configuration_id\":\"A1_COUPLED\",\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"input_result_id\":\"RESULT-013\",\"output_sha256\":\"5e6fed2db016c7e2bf5253070249e045bb8dcda18136cd77d6c378709727b5f1\",\"schema\":\"artifact-coupled-maintenance-rejection-v0\",\"validation_code\":\"token_budget_exceeded\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","has_new_line":false,"truncated":false,"stop_type":"eos","stopping_word":"","tokens_ca